        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "b670d82c-ade6-5a95-8b69-8889eadfc377",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stephen Cepello, Jesse Ventura, Mark Dayton, Steve Strong, Steve Barkley\n- Places: Minnesota\n- Roles: Governor of Minnesota, wrestler, artist, comedian\n- Works: Elephant Parts, Rio, Cruisin'\n- Topics: portrait painting, Minnesota politics, comedy music videos\n\nFacts:\n- After retiring from wrestling to focus on his art career, Stephen Cepello was selected to paint the official Governor's Mansion and Minnesota State Capitol portraits of former wrestler and Governor of Minnesota Jesse Ventura.\n- \"Elephant Parts\" is a one-hour work with parody commercials, comedy sketches, and five full-length music videos.\n- The music videos in \"Elephant Parts\" include the popular songs \"Rio\" and \"Cruisin'.\"\n- \"Cruisin'\" featured wrestler Steve Strong and Monterey-based comic Steve Barkley, who was known as \"Chicago\" Steve Barkley.\n- Mark Dayton of the Democratic-Farmer-Labor Party was the current Governor of Minnesota in the cited sentence.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
